      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/as-pure-s/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The first differences are 5, 9, 13 and 7, 11, 15; both sets of second differences are four. Comparing with 2𝑛2 = 2, 8, 18, 32, … gives the corrections −1, −2, −3, −4 and 1, 2, 3, 4. Replacing 𝑛by 𝑚+ 1 in the first sequence gives (𝑚+ 1)(2𝑚+ 1); taking 𝑛= 𝑚in the second gives 𝑚(2𝑚+ 1), exactly the factors above.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
